> Module Educator_adjustment

# Educator expenses adjustment (Schedule 1 line 11)

Direct File module `educatorAdjustment.xml`. Issue #24. Tests are in
`catala/tests/test_educator_adjustment.catala_en`; the oracle comparison is
`make difftest SCOPE=educator_adjustment` (`difftest/mappings/educator_adjustment.mjs`).

> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

## 26 U.S.C. § 62(a)(2)(D) Certain expenses of elementary and secondary school teachers

"The deductions allowed by section 162 which consist of expenses, not in
excess of $250, paid or incurred by an eligible educator— (i) by reason of the
participation of the educator in professional development courses related to
the curriculum in which the educator provides instruction or to the students
for which the educator provides instruction, and (ii) in connection with
books, supplies (other than nonathletic supplies for courses of instruction in
health or physical education), computer equipment (including related software
and services) and other equipment, and supplementary materials used by the
eligible educator in the classroom." (`sources/statute/irc-62.html`)

The $250 is indexed. For TY2024 it is $300: "for taxable years beginning in
2024, under § 62(a)(2)(D) the amount of the deduction allowed under § 162 ...
is $300." (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.13, `sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` p 11.)
The constant is `P.educator_expense_cap_per_educator`.

## Form 1040 instructions, Schedule 1 line 11

"If you were an eligible educator in 2024, you can deduct on line 11 up to $300
of qualified expenses you paid in 2024. If you and your spouse are filing
jointly and both of you were eligible educators, the maximum deduction is $600.
However, neither spouse can deduct more than $300 of their qualified expenses
on line 11." (`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 89.)

## Direct File rules reproduced

- `/wasK12Educators` is an enumeration `tpDid`, `spouseDid`, `bothDid`,
  `neither` (`/k12EducatorOptions`). The flow only offers `spouseDid` and
  `bothDid` on a joint return; the facts `/tpWasK12Educator` and
  `/spouseWasK12Educator` themselves do not test the filing status, so neither
  does this module (inputs are complete, CONVENTIONS section 3).
- Each educator's amount is `LesserOf(300, expenses)`; an educator who is not
  flagged contributes $0 whatever the expenses box holds.
- `/educatorExpensesAdjustment` is `Round` of the sum, and `$0` for a filer who
  is an MFJ dependent (`/isMFJDependent`, `filers.xml`).

```catala-metadata
## The `/k12EducatorOptions` answer. DF: educatorAdjustment.xml `/wasK12Educators`.
declaration enumeration K12EducatorOptions:
  -- TpDid
  -- SpouseDid
  -- BothDid
  -- Neither

## Schedule 1 line 11. DF: educatorAdjustment.xml.
declaration scope EducatorAdjustment:
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /wasK12Educators (Writable)
  input was_k12_educators content K12EducatorOptions
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /primaryEducatorExpensesWritable
  input primary_educator_expenses_writable content money
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /secondaryEducatorExpensesWritable
  input secondary_educator_expenses_writable content money
  # DF: filers.xml /isMFJDependent, from Filers.is_mfj_dependent
  input is_mfj_dependent condition

  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /tpWasK12Educator
  output tp_was_k12_educator condition
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /spouseWasK12Educator
  output spouse_was_k12_educator condition
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /primaryEducatorExpenses
  output primary_educator_expenses content money
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /secondaryEducatorExpenses
  output secondary_educator_expenses content money
  # Schedule 1 line 11. DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /educatorExpensesAdjustment
  output educator_expenses_adjustment content money
  # DF: educatorAdjustment.xml /isReceivingEducatorExpensesAdjustment
  output is_receiving_educator_expenses_adjustment condition
```

## Who is an eligible educator

```catala
scope EducatorAdjustment:
  # IRC 62(a)(2)(D) "eligible educator"; DF: /tpWasK12Educator
  definition tp_was_k12_educator equals
    was_k12_educators = BothDid or was_k12_educators = TpDid

  # DF: /spouseWasK12Educator
  definition spouse_was_k12_educator equals
    was_k12_educators = BothDid or was_k12_educators = SpouseDid
```

## The $300 cap per educator

```catala
scope EducatorAdjustment:
  # IRC 62(a)(2)(D), Rev. Proc. 2023-34 p 11; DF: /primaryEducatorExpenses
  definition primary_educator_expenses equals
    if tp_was_k12_educator then
      Money.min of P.educator_expense_cap_per_educator,
                   primary_educator_expenses_writable
    else $0

  # DF: /secondaryEducatorExpenses
  definition secondary_educator_expenses equals
    if spouse_was_k12_educator then
      Money.min of P.educator_expense_cap_per_educator,
                   secondary_educator_expenses_writable
    else $0
```

## Schedule 1 line 11

"Educator expenses" is the sum of both educators' capped amounts (at most $600
on a joint return). A filer who is only on a joint return as the dependent of
another taxpayer (`/isMFJDependent`) gets nothing.

```catala
scope EducatorAdjustment:
  # Sch 1 line 11, f1040s1--2024.pdf p 1. DF: /educatorExpensesAdjustment
  definition educator_expenses_adjustment equals
    if is_mfj_dependent then $0
    else R.round_dollar of (primary_educator_expenses
                            + secondary_educator_expenses)

  # DF: /isReceivingEducatorExpensesAdjustment
  definition is_receiving_educator_expenses_adjustment equals
    educator_expenses_adjustment > $0
```
